     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-k, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5288\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to desig-\nnating a portion of the state highway system as \"Melvin Harris, Jr. Way\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo designate portion of the state highway as \"Melvin Harris, Jr. Way\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section to the highway law to designate portion of\nstate route one hundred two in hamlet of Uniondale, Nassau County as\n\"Melvin Harris, Jr. Way\".\n\nSection 2 states that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nthe installation and maintenance of signing of the highway.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs a Commissioner for the Nassau County Commission on Human Rights and\nPresident of the Hempstead Chapter of the NAACP, Mr. Melvin Harris Jr.\nadvocated passionately for positive change; he fought for inclusion,\nopportunity and upward mobility for the underserved and the disenfran-\nchised. Melvin's goal was to make the vision of Martin Luther King, Jr.\na reality in Nassau County, where every resident is given the opportu-\nnity to achieve his or her full potential. As Vice President of the\nUniondale Community Council and subsequently as President of the Nost-\nrand Gardens Civic Association, Melvin advocated strongly for the Union-\ndale community.\n\nAs Union Chairman of the Queens Village Depot, New York City Transit\nAuthority and Political Director for the Amalgamated Transit Union Local\n1056, Melvin advocated for worker's rights. In 2016 the City of New York\nrenamed 222st in Queens Village, \"Melvin Harris, Jr. Way\" honoring him\nfor his tireless work and dedication to Queens County and the New York\nCity Metropolitan Transit Authority.\n\nPatty Harris, the wife of Melvin, has requested Front Street be renamed\nbecause it is the street nearest to the Harris home.The Executive Board\nand Members of the Nostrand Gardens Civic Association, in unity with the\nresidents of Uniondale also advocated that the deserving and distin-\nguished honor be bestowed upon Melvin Harris, Jr.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
